Z||000005||batboy||05-09-2000||11:52 AM||||The Fiero automatic trannies (TH125) have a lock up torque converter. Buy the one you like best, little grasshopper, that one will make you most happy. Of course the 88 GT will probably hold it's value the best, but how well was it maintained compared to the others?||||reg||1
Z||000006||RiceCooker||05-09-2000||02:39 PM||||If you plan on autocrossing at all, you should definitely go with the 88. I've never driven one, but from what I've heard the handling is that much better and certainly the car does have a lot more potential.<P>If I was being biased i would say *NO QUESTION, 86SE!!!* (that's what i got)||||reg||1
